cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the associated paper."
title: "GSN-Adaptive-Kalman-Streamflow: adaptive Kalman filtering for Generalized Shot Noise streamflow models, with application to the Camastra basin"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB implementation of an adaptive Kalman filter for Generalized Shot
  Noise streamflow models, with recursive Sage-Husa estimation of the
  measurement and process-noise covariances. The process-noise update
  includes a correction for the covariance propagated through the state
  dynamics, NIS-normalized forgetting weights, a bootstrap initialization of
  the measurement-noise variance and a prediction-only treatment of missing
  observations. The code applies the filter to 37 years of daily inflow
  observations of the Camastra reservoir (southern Italy) under two
  rainfall configurations, a synthetic effective-rainfall realization used
  as deterministic input and rainfall absorbed as adaptive process noise,
  and evaluates accuracy, consistency and predictive-band coverage.
